{
 "_doc": "Bugle and drum calls of the Union infantry (Casey 1862, vol. 1, 'Instruction for the drum-major') with the Hardee 1861 list as second witness. NAMES AND ORDER are documented: read from the OCR of the two manuals by tools/bt/drill_*.py and checked by drill_check.py (drill/DRILL-HARDEE-NOTES.md section 2; items HAR-L01, HAR-L02, HAR-L03, HCS-L01..L05). The MUSICAL NOTATION is not in the OCR text and was not transcribed: 'notation' is null for every call. Casey's printed leaf for the bugle calls (printed p. 229-230 of vol. 1, archive.org infantrytacticsf01brig) is not at leaf offset +59 as for the text pages: 32 plates are interleaved, so the page images must be located by the leaf search described in AUDIO3D-NOTES.md before transcription. Until then the engine plays modern recordings of the call of the same name where a licensed one exists (real_standin, never claimed as the 1863 call) and nothing otherwise. Taps (Butterfield, July 1862) is a call of the Army of the Potomac not in the 1862 manuals.",
 "tier_names": "documented (primary manual text, OCR-verified)",
